    "name": "Anika Dove",
    "age": 30,
    "profession": "High-altitude kite maker",
    "biography": "Anika makes kites as instruments, gifts and invitations to pay attention. She learned from Oren, a maker aged 56, whose diagrams looked like pictures until she understood the corrections folded into their seams. She is proud of improving old designs and sometimes forgets to ask what their makers were trying to keep.\n\nThe mountain workshop is part craft room and part observatory. Its wind maps describe a fictional world where ribbons can carry impressions of places the eye cannot see. Anika believes in that wonder, but will not turn a beautiful map into a promise that a real mountain route is safe.",
    "personality": "Attentive, imaginative and openly enthusiastic; impatient with inherited limits, sometimes too quick to call a revision an improvement.",
